// Rimewake A: the land, the one source for both the terrain art and the collision mask.
//
// World pixels, y down. Each island is a closed chain of cubic Béziers (two control points, then
// the end), run clockwise on screen: walkable `Top`s left to right, then `Rock` down the far side,
// under the water along the keel and back up. The sea's surface is y = 712 (drawn in
// background.svg; terrain.svg tints the ice below it); every gap between floes runs to the bottom
// of the map, so whoever falls in is lost. Tops are roughened less than rock would be (`rough`),
// since ice is smoother, and capped with snow. `dress` places decorations into the map's
// terrain.svg, one rule per slot (`{{name}}`).
//
// This file was laid out from key points (the east half mirrors the west, with its own keels) and
// is the source from here on: edit it by hand.
